{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1660,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We know that Jupiter has an atmosphere made\nup mainly of hydrogen and helium. Europa,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6180,
    "dDurationMs": 6270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a moon of Jupiter, has a very thin oxygen\natmosphere, and HD 209458 b, a Jupiter-sized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12450,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exoplanet orbiting the star HD 209458 which\nis 154 lightyears away, has an atmosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18250,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that contains hydrogen, carbon, oxygen, sodium,\ncarbon dioxide, methane, and even water vapor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23410,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All this even though we haven’t visited\nany of these places to directly sample the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26710,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "air... but we don’t need to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28500,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can study the air on other planets, moons,\nand exoplanets just by looking at them. In"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33300,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particular, by looking at light that bounces\noff or passes through their atmospheres, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37670,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you shine light on a gas, the molecules\nabsorb and scatter different frequencies of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42100,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that light in different amounts. If we then\nsplit the transmitted or scattered light apart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46550,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into its constituent colors using a prism\nor diffraction grating, we can see a molecule’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51600,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light-absorption fingerprint, or its light-emission\nfingerprint. This is hydrogen. This is nitrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57640,
    "dDurationMs": 3189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oxygen. Methane. Carbon dioxide. Water. Sulfuric\nacid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60829,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when we look at the sunlight bouncing off\nof the atmospheres of planets and notice spikes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64449,
    "dDurationMs": 3821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of certain heights in certain frequencies,\nwe can carefully match those to the known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68270,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fingerprints of gas molecules, and learn not\njust what gases make up the air, but even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73080,
    "dDurationMs": 950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their relative abundances!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74030,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, we don’t even need to be able to\nsee a planet at all to learn about its atmosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78050,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– many exoplanets have been discovered\nbecause they pass in front of their parent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81910,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "star, which we see as a dip in the overall\nintensity of the star’s light. But if an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exoplanet has an atmosphere, the gas molecules\nin its atmosphere will block some frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90360,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an extra amount, according to their molecular\nfingerprints, and we can do the same gas-matching"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94860,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "process as before. And that’s how we know\nwhat’s in the atmosphere of HD 209458 b!."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99910,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, in practice it’s pretty darn\nchallenging to use molecular fingerprints"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104060,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to study exoplanet atmospheres, because air\nis thin so the fingerprints are super faint"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108330,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we need big sensitive telescopes and spectrometers;\nand because atmospheres are complicated and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their fingerprints can be ambiguous or hard\nto match; and because different parts of a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116840,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single star emit different amounts of different\ncolors of light, so a planet’s effect on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120890,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the star’s spectrum will depend on which\npart the planet passes in front of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124680,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But all of these difficulties can be dealt\nwith by clever astronomers, and thus we have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128420,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been able to figure out what the air is like\non planets hundreds of light years away that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132790,
    "dDurationMs": 29320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can’t even see."
    } ]
  } ]
}
